<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-15986] .NET: ClientConnectionTest.TestFailover is flaky</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-15986</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;ClientConnectionTest.TestFailover is flaky:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
Expected: instance of &amp;lt;&lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;System&lt;/span&gt;.Exception&amp;gt;
  But was:  &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;
   at Apache.Ignite.Core.Tests.Client.ClientConnectionTest.TestFailover() in /opt/buildagent/work/7bc1c54bc719b67c/modules/platforms/dotnet/Apache.Ignite.Core.Tests/Client/ClientConnectionTest.cs:line 618
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The reason is that sometimes the client detects connection failure in the background with OnAffinityTopologyVersionChange callback.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
